ines near 23.3\u00b0, 32.6\u00b0 and 33.45\u00b0 do not match the observed peaks at 31.1\u00b0 and 31.85\u00b0.\n- **ZnFe(SiO3)2 (pyroxene):** I compared it with typical clinopyroxene lines (strong ~29.8\u00b0, 30.5\u00b0, ~35.5\u00b0) rather than computing them. The 30.5\u00b0 and 35.5\u00b0 lines are absent; I did not check 29.8\u00b0 individually.\n- **Er2Cu(GeO3)4:** this was not computed; it is excluded only because the brownmillerite indexing leaves no peaks unexplained.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-1105158\"], \"confidence\": 0.85, \"note\": \"All main peaks (29.85, 31.1, 31.85, 43.65, 47.65, 22.95, 24.45, 21.45) index to the Sr2ScGaO5 brownmillerite cell (5.76 x 5.98 x 15.27 A) with no unexplained main reflections.\"}",
